asdcontrol (0.6.0-0oaxaca1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Initial Oaxaca package of asdcontrol 0.6.0 (roadmap step 6).
    Omarchy v4.0.4 installs asdcontrol, and the desktop's
    oaxaca-brightness-display-apple script (Omarchy's
    omarchy-brightness-display-apple, renamed) runs "sudo asdcontrol" to read
    and set the brightness of an Apple Studio Display or Pro Display XDR over
    USB HID. Ubuntu's archive has no asdcontrol.
  * The upstream tarball is the GitHub release tag; see the "upstream" file
    next to debian/.
  * d/asdcontrol.sudoers, installed as /etc/sudoers.d/50-asdcontrol (mode
    0440): Omarchy's rule (omacom/omarchy-pkgs, pkgbuilds/asdcontrol/
    asdcontrol.sudoers) with %sudo in place of %wheel, Ubuntu's admin group.
    The rule lets members of the sudo group run only the three asdcontrol
    invocations the brightness script uses, without a password.
  * d/rules: the upstream Makefile links without LDFLAGS, so the rules file
    passes dpkg's CPPFLAGS and LDFLAGS through CXXFLAGS for hardening.

 -- santisbon <santisbon@users.noreply.github.com>  Sat, 10 Oct 2026 12:00:00 -0500
